    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "The equation is not signposted for factorising. The student must see that 3x+15 factorises as 3(x+5), match the common factor (x+5) on both sides, and equate m-4 to 3. This reframes an equation containing x as a structural comparison of factors, and expanding and equating coefficients is an alternative route. It is one short chain of linked steps. It is more demanding than the scaffolded area-to-width factorising in p15-q11 and the single formula-building step in A3. It is below the multi-case listing and optimising in A4.",
